07:14:24 run E20 20260918-071424: Aquatic rotation for a year on LAKE (E25: a live lake edge). Only the water layer managed: every in-embark water entry allowed and assigned by the matrix, groups, coupling and ecology off, rotation enabled. 404,000 ticks (a year), two replicates. Every 15,000 ticks the wild feature-layer units are counted by species and the fort's living citizens are counted. Questions: does an assigned water species ever arrive outside its seasons; when a species goes out of season, do its fish leave the map or die in place. Moved here from OCEAN2, where the seven-dwarf fort was wiped out by the map's own saltwater crocodiles three seasons into the year, twice, ending the game.
